Fix DECSED indexing a line-relative pointer with an absolute buffer offset

BuffSelectedEraseCurToEnd() and BuffSelectedEraseHomeToCur() -- the two halves
of DECSED, CSI ? Ps J -- both take

    buff_char_t *CodeLineW = &CodeBuffW[LinePtr];

which is the base of the CURSOR'S LINE, and then index it with `j`, which is an
ABSOLUTE buffer offset:

  buffer.c:BuffSelectedEraseCurToEnd()
      TmpPtr = GetLinePtr(PageStart+CursorY);
      for (i = CursorY ; i <= YEnd ; i++) {
          for (j = TmpPtr + offset; j < TmpPtr + NumOfColumns - offset; j++) {
              if (!(CodeLineW[j].attr2 & Attr2Protect)) {     /* <-- */
                  BuffSetChar(&CodeBuffW[j], 0x20, 'H');      /* correct */
                  CodeLineW[j].attr &= AttrSgrMask;           /* <-- */
              }
          }
          offset = 0;
          TmpPtr = NextLinePtr(TmpPtr);
      }

So `CodeLineW[j]` is `CodeBuffW[LinePtr + j]`, roughly twice as far into the
buffer as intended. Three consequences:

1. The protect bit is read from the WRONG CELL, so DECSED erases protected
   characters and preserves unprotected ones, which is the whole of what the
   sequence is for.

2. `CodeLineW[j].attr &= AttrSgrMask` MODIFIES that wrong cell -- unrelated
   scrollback loses its attributes.

3. `LinePtr` and `TmpPtr` each range up to BufferSize - NumOfColumns, so their
   sum reaches nearly twice BufferSize. Once the page has been scrolled into
   the second half of the ring, the access is past the end of the allocation.
   Both the read and the read-modify-write are out of bounds, and both indices
   come off the wire: CUP places the cursor and any output scrolls the page.

BuffSelectedEraseHomeToCur() has the same wrong base on its protect test; its
writes already use CodeBuffW[j].

BuffSelectedEraseCurToEnd() has a second, independent defect in the same loop:

    for (j = TmpPtr + offset; j < TmpPtr + NumOfColumns - offset; j++)

`offset` is the start column and is subtracted from the END bound as well, so
on the cursor's own line the loop covers NumOfColumns - 2*CursorX cells instead
of NumOfColumns - CursorX, and covers nothing at all once the cursor is past
the middle of the screen. `offset` is zeroed for every later line, so only the
first is affected.

Reproduction, via the Sterna oracle (vtterm.c + buffer.c headless). Four
lines of "aaaaPPPPcccc" where PPPP is written under DECSCA 1, then DECSED 0
from row 2 column 7:

    printf '...' | oracle --cols 12 --rows 4 --attrs

    before:                       after:
      0 |aaaaPPPPcccc|              0 |aaaaPPPPcccc|
      1 |aaaaPPPPcccc|              1 |aaaaPPPP    |
      2 |    PPPP    |              2 |    PPPP    |
      3 |            |              3 |    PPPP    |

Row 1 is the cursor's row and is untouched, because of defect 2. Row 3's
protected run is erased, because its protect bits were read from a line that is
off the screen entirely.

And under AddressSanitizer, with the page scrolled down the ring first
(200 line feeds, then CUP to row 20 column 40, then CSI ? 0 J):

    ==737980==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
    READ of size 1 at 0x7f56375fee33 thread T0
        #0 BuffSelectedEraseCurToEnd buffer.c:5491
        #1 CSQSelScreenErase vtterm.c:1773
        #2 CSQuest vtterm.c:3245
        #3 ParseCS vtterm.c:4127
    0x7f56375fee33 is located 51 bytes after 448000-byte region
    allocated by ChangeBuffer buffer.c:522

CSI ? 1 J reaches the same overflow with other cursor positions.

Found by diffing DECSED against a reimplementation with the sterna
differential harness. Tera Term 5.7.0-dev (commit 827a35b05).

--- a/teraterm/teraterm/buffer.c
+++ b/teraterm/teraterm/buffer.c
@@ -5488,10 +5488,10 @@ void BuffSelectedEraseCurToEnd(void)
 	for (i = CursorY ; i <= YEnd ; i++) {
-		for (j = TmpPtr + offset; j < TmpPtr + NumOfColumns - offset; j++) {
-			if (!(CodeLineW[j].attr2 & Attr2Protect)) {
+		for (j = TmpPtr + offset; j < TmpPtr + NumOfColumns; j++) {
+			if (!(CodeBuffW[j].attr2 & Attr2Protect)) {
 				BuffSetChar(&CodeBuffW[j], 0x20, 'H');
-				CodeLineW[j].attr &= AttrSgrMask;
+				CodeBuffW[j].attr &= AttrSgrMask;
 			}
 		}
 		offset = 0;
@@ -5531,7 +5531,7 @@ void BuffSelectedEraseHomeToCur(void)
 		for (j = TmpPtr; j < TmpPtr + offset; j++) {
-			if (!(CodeLineW[j].attr2 & Attr2Protect)) {
+			if (!(CodeBuffW[j].attr2 & Attr2Protect)) {
 				BuffSetChar(&CodeBuffW[j], 0x20, 'H');
 				CodeBuffW[j].attr &= AttrSgrMask;
 			}
